{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01BJCn3yXW1Ck73vcDDuDS3q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a personal productivity/R&D command system for J.C. Liechty. Grounded from the project docs and code:\n\n- **It's a single-folder, markdown-backed productivity system.** Everything lives in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` â€” tasks, projects, inbox, and archives are plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, etc.) that are the source of truth. No database, no syncing, no binary formats.\n\n- **It ships a local web app, `anchor_gui.py`** (the one declared deliverable) â€” a stdlib-only Python HTTP server that renders an interactive dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, reading and writing the markdown directly. It runs persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. A CLI engine (`anchor.py`) mirrors the same logic and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Core task management:** tasks move through a lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored) across per-domain files (academic, commercial, family, writing). The GUI exposes add/capture/edit/done/cancel/save endpoints; a 5:00 AM `anchor_healthcheck.py` self-test verifies file integrity and every endpoint daily.\n\n- **Its major build effort is an embedded R&D \"cockpit\"** for running the planning trio â€” **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman**. Each project gets a window where the lanes (Research Â· Planning Â· Build Â· Deliverables Â· Grass) show their most-recent session as a status-lit tile that expands inline into a summary + a real terminal.\n\n- **The R&D surface ships in versioned waves, the latest being v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (built, 9 waves GREEN / 637 tests passed, merged to master `38fd70e`). It adds: real **ConPTY terminals** with per-session git-worktree isolation (the one waived native dep, `pywinpty`), a skill-auto-loads-once seed, a Claudeâ†”Gemini engine toggle, cached/validated session+project summaries, cost/tokens/time rollups, grass-idea promotion, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **Branding:** presented as a **Ghost World Labs** tool \"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\", using the vendored brand mark as favicon and masthead lockup.\n\nThe North Star throughout: make each project's window a calm, single-screen cockpit where opening a session \"feels exactly like a normal Claude Code / Gemini session\" â€” skill loads once, greets once, no repeating-prompt loop."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24714,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24714},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9d022c9-f18f-48f5-8a27-e7b244e501d1","uuid":"63002567-ca77-426a-8f6f-71b73ef26d50","request_id":"req_011Cc1JGgZNQsvyyBhspf4A8"}
